From 5fd0c14841b2536a006fd2655a111a13da4ff585 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:30:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/49] x86_64/fpu/587: keep the x87 exp, exp2, log, log2 and
 pow

Since 2.28/2.29 the dbl-64 versions are new C implementations with new
symbol versions and no wrappers, which the x87 versions (__ieee754_*) do
not provide.  Do what i386 does: keep the x87 code with the classic
wrappers and empty the dbl-64 data tables, so libm keeps the old symbol
versions of these functions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
